{"timestamp":"2026-05-04T22:28:39.944Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"::code-comment{title=\"[P1] Interrupted multi-session migrations can stay incomplete\" body=\"The rerun path only scans sessions already present in the v2 summary. If the first run is interrupted after writing session 0 to /main but before writing later v1 sessions, the rerun treats the checkpoint as existing and never compares against the v1 session list, so those missing sessions are never copied into v2.\" file=\"/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go\" start=1129 end=1137 priority=1 confidence=0.9}\n\n::code-comment{title=\"[P2] Legacy full.jsonl is treated as complete v2 data\" body=\"This makes reruns skip checkpoints whose /full artifacts are still stored as full.jsonl/content_hash.txt. That avoids duplicate generations, but it leaves full.jsonl in v2 permanently, which contradicts the stated requirement that v2 should use raw_transcript/raw_transcript_hash.txt instead.\" file=\"/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/v2_committed.go\" start=175 end=190 priority=2 confidence=0.93}\n\n**Findings**\nThe main idempotent rerun path is much better for the simple case, and the targeted tests pass. But I found two requirement gaps:\n\n1. Interrupted multi-session checkpoint migrations can be left incomplete. The existing-v2 branch checks only `len(v2Summary.Sessions)`, so it can repair raw artifacts for sessions already known to v2, but cannot discover v1 sessions that never made it into `/main`.\n\n2. The legacy filename handling conflicts with “full.jsonl should not be in v2.” The code now recognizes legacy `full.jsonl` as valid and skips, but does not rename or clean it up. A safe fix would likely distinguish “complete enough to avoid repacking” from “needs filename normalization.”\n\n**Verification**\nI ran:\n\n```sh\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestMigrateCheckpointsV2_(RerunResumesInterruptedMigration|RerunSkipsLegacyArchivedFullJsonl|RerunPicksUpNewV1Checkpoints|ForceOverwritesExisting|ForceMultipleCheckpoints|AllSkippedOnRerun)$'\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli -run TestMigrate\n```\n\nThe targeted suite passed.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
